 "fixed_bug_90mhz": {
  "note": "At 90 MHz the cycle period (11111.1 ps) is not a whole number of 1 ps units, so each wait rounded differently and two events of the same cycle could compare unequal: a transfer engine register write due at cycle N was not yet committed when an MMA read the register at cycle N (llama_prefill/tiny gave NaN outputs with the timeline memory). Fixed in include/tnca_model.hpp Context: the period is rounded once to whole resolution units (11111 ps); every model time is an integral number of cycles. Configs at 100 MHz (exact) are unaffected."
 }
